# GitNexus index after commit

The graph is a snapshot. `impact`, `query`, `context`, and `api_impact`
only see the last `analyze`. Commits and files after that snapshot are
invisible until re-index.

## After `git commit` or `git merge`

Run from the repo root as soon as the commit succeeds (do not skip):

```bash
node .gitnexus/run.cjs analyze --index-only
```

If `.gitnexus/run.cjs` is missing:

```bash
npx gitnexus analyze --index-only
```

Then read `gitnexus://repo/Sangiaodich/context` and confirm it is not
behind HEAD. Only then run `detect_changes` if the commit protocol
requires it.

Do **not** run `analyze` inside a git hook with a short timeout — it can
corrupt the KuzuDB index. The agent runs it in the terminal after the
commit. `--index-only` is the default after commit; full `analyze` (no
flag) only when the generated GitNexus blocks in AGENTS.md / CLAUDE.md
must be regenerated.

## Before trusting the graph

If context reports stale, or `.gitnexus/meta.json` `lastCommit` ≠ HEAD,
re-index before `impact` / `query` / `context`. A missing symbol in a
stale index means "not indexed yet", not "unused".
